<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $145.6 mln Nov 1.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $145.6 mln Nov 1.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $145.6 million surplus on November 1, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 1</p>
<p>Exports: $232.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $157.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $303.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $233 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $145.6 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
